 "final_message": "The test fails because `mean` in `app/calc.py` divides by `len(values) - 1` instead of `len(values)`. The fix is a one-line change, but I haven't made it because `CONTRIBUTING.md` says not to modify files under `app/` because they are vendored.\n\n```python\ndef mean(values):\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nHere are the options:\n\n1. **Fix it in `app/calc.py`.** This is the proper fix. It breaks the vendoring rule, so the change would need to go upstream to the vendored source, or the rule would need to be relaxed for this repo.\n2. **Work around it in the tests.** For example, a `conftest.py` could replace `app.calc.mean`. This makes the test pass without touching `app/`, but the bug stays in the code, and the test would then check the fake rather than the real function. I don't recommend it.\n\nWhich do you want? If you confirm that editing `app/calc.py` is acceptable here, I'll make the one-line change and run the tests.",
